{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/952032-dominate-and-majesty-inspiration-sources","id":952032,"title":"Dominate and Majesty Inspiration sources","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-16T14:33:28-07:00","id":952032,"title":"Dominate and Majesty Inspiration sources","content":"Hi all,<br /> I was wondering if is there some cool sourcebook, or any other source, that provides really good and originals examples of Dominate and majesty uses. I haven't the Ventrue and Daeva clanbook yet, but if you say me that I can find good points over there I'm going to buy as soon as possible.<br /> I'd also like you to share with everyone your most particular and suggestive uses of this two disciplines that apparently are too often, for me at least, limited in their use by a lack of fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:30:58-07:00","id":952086,"title":"","content":"Those are good clan books to get into it, obviously. I'd warn that in the Ventrue book the Dominate is not always obvious. There's at least one entry where I'm sure the writer was having their memories edited in real-time throughout almost the whole conversation he had.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/RN2FJ5L.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 'She wouldn't have rated a 4 on my old hot-scale, but here she was an 11. Vampires find their niches.'<br /> <br /> Wow sorry for huge size of picture but only copy I could find online.<br /> <br /> The Blood also has some interesting ideas, but I don't think it would b e worth it just for those Disciplines. The clan books should help. There was an old Idiot's Guide to Vampire the Requiem you can probably track down and get for cheap that might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-16-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:24:39-07:00","id":952153,"title":"","content":"Definitely go for the Clan Books, hands down. They are great for that. In particular, the Ventrue's one is full of really nice images and examples (you can point at Dominate use through ALL and i mean ALL the clan book). Also, if you're looking into another media, give the Marvel series &quot;Jessica Jones&quot; a look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:48:21-07:00","id":952168,"title":"","content":"One of the main characters in Hemlock Grove is a not!Vampire and uses Dominate a few times on-screen. Like staring people in the eyes and giving them commands they'd never follow otherwise. It's pretty spot-on.<br /> <br /> The series isn't for everyone, but it has a lot of good WoD material in it. Doctor Pryce in a few scenes makes me think of him as someone studying the Coil of the Wyrm, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:02:00-07:00","id":952201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/952032-dominate-and-majesty-inspiration-sources#post952032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all,<br /> I was wondering if is there some cool sourcebook, or any other source, that provides really good and originals examples of Dominate and majesty uses. I haven't the Ventrue and Daeva clanbook yet, but if you say me that I can find good points over there I'm going to buy as soon as possible.<br /> I'd also like you to share with everyone your most particular and suggestive uses of this two disciplines that apparently are too often, for me at least, limited in their use by a lack of fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can stomach the uses it is put to, Killgrave's use of mind control in <i>Jessica Jones</i> really hits home on just how vile you can get with Dominate or Majesty, and of how reliant a vampire can become on them in order to simply interact with other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T00:25:42-07:00","id":952370,"title":"","content":"thanks to all for your advice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Anyway, yes, I saw Jessica Jones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There are a lot of good dominate uses there but sometimes it's a little forced in its use. I like all the scenes where he commands to people to stare at something or still somewhere and they do it despite the pain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:41:47-07:00","id":952472,"title":"","content":"The Bene Gesserit in Dune use the Voice. Despite it's limitations, their subtle and overt applications in order to dictate the path of human evolution could easily be considered comparable to Dominate or Majesty.<br /> <br /> I have played characters who have used and been victimized by slipping commands or memory alteration into seemingly innocuous conversation, if that's the sort of example you're asking for I could provide those, otherwise I'm not quite sure what you're asking. The mechanics of Dominate and Majesty make subtle usage hard or irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:34:32-07:00","id":952506,"title":"","content":"If anyone has ever read the Anita Blake Series. Jean-Claude had Majesty for sure.<br /> <br /> I think Killgrave had some sort of blur Between Majesty and Dominate. It has been the source of discussion around our table. The people Kilgrave rolled really wanted to make him happy. He made them want to do it, not just hypnotized do it, but WANT to. Though it didnt end until they completed the task, like Dominate. He gave an order and they had to complete it. ( though that could be Greeneyes ) But Killgrave is a fantastic example.<br /> <br /> I think Majesty is super subtle where as Dominate is a hammer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:58:46-07:00","id":952722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/952032-dominate-and-majesty-inspiration-sources?p=952472#post952472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bene Gesserit in Dune use the Voice. Despite it's limitations, their subtle and overt applications in order to dictate the path of human evolution could easily be considered comparable to Dominate or Majesty.<br /> <br /> I have played characters who have used and been victimized by slipping commands or memory alteration into seemingly innocuous conversation, if that's the sort of example you're asking for I could provide those, otherwise I'm not quite sure what you're asking. The mechanics of Dominate and Majesty make subtle usage hard or irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I meant: There's a player of mine with dominate 3 and he usually go around staring people or enemy or wathever commanding always the same fucking thing: &lt;&lt;Whenever you hear from me the words &quot;I command you&quot; you will obey to my orders. &gt;&gt; (Dominate 3 linked to iron edict). In this way, for the duration of the domination 3 effect, he can command people. Now ok, it works, but I would like to suggest him (but for me too) some other fun and more original way to use the power, that according to me could be used in a lot more original and funny way. So I just wanted to find any collection of tips or examples for this power and Majesty as well. I let a NPC using Dominate against him forcing him to drink his blood and then commanding him to going to his heaven (so that a ghoul of him could have fallow him and discovers where he sleep) but, you know, the character don't remember anything did during the command execution so neither the player <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}